&lt;li&gt;Prepare job evaluations, salary surveys, and job architecture to keep leveling and pay structures current&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain salary structures and salary budgets in partnership with Finance and People leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with line management to assess competitive labor market trends and inform pay decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain working knowledge of federal and state compensation legislation to ensure compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own incentive, stock option, and bonus plan design and administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner on performance management systems and HRIS/UKG compensation workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select, develop, and manage a high-performing Total Rewards team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience leading compensation or total rewards functions, ideally at a Director level or above&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of compensation philosophy, market benchmarking, and job architecture design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing bonus, incentive, and equity program design and administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with compensation-related federal and state regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong partnership skills — this role works closely with Finance, People leadership, and business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
