&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideal locations- Mclean, VA, San Francisco Bay Area, and New York, NY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ID.me is seeking a dynamic Sales Director to lead and grow our Commercial and Workforce Identity Solutions business. This is a fully remote leadership role responsible for managing a small initial team of Account Executives and Account Managers driving new logo acquisition and net revenue retention (NRR) growth within existing accounts. The team is expected to scale quickly, making a growth mindset and proven experience building in high-growth environments essential. Experience in cybersecurity or identity solutions is highly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervisory Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage, mentor, and develop an initial team of AEs and AMs, with the expectation of rapid team growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear performance expectations, conduct regular pipeline reviews, and deliver ongoing coaching to accelerate team development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale repeatable playbooks and processes to support a growing distributed sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Revenue Operations, Marketing, and Product to align go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of accountability, continuous learning, and growth mindset across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and exceed quota targets for new business acquisition (new logo) and net revenue retention across existing commercial and workforce identity accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a strategic territory plan targeting mid-market and enterprise organizations seeking identity verification and workforce identity solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex, consultative sales cycles from prospecting through close, engaging executive-level stakeholders (CISO, CIO, VP HR, VP IT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive expansion and upsell motions within the existing customer base to grow NRR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately forecast pipeline and revenue on a weekly, monthly, and quarterly basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Product, and Legal to drive deals to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent ID.me at industry events, conferences, and customer engagements as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide market and competitive intelligence to inform product and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and prepare for rapid headcount and territory growth, scaling team structure proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills / Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of SaaS sales experience with a demonstrated ability to close complex enterprise deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a sales leadership role managing and developing quota-carrying AEs and/or AMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of meeting or exceeding individual and team revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into commercial or enterprise accounts with multi-stakeholder buying processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong growth mindset with demonstrated experience scaling teams, processes, and playbooks in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in pipeline management and forecasting methodologies (e.g., MEDDIC, MEDDPICC); Salesforce CRM preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, negotiation, and executive presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and effectively in a fully remote environment while managing a distributed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The qualifications below are ideal, but not all are required. We encourage candidates to apply if they satisfy some, but not all of these qualifications.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in cybersecurity, identity and access management (IAM), or digital identity solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling workforce identity, SSO, MFA, or identity verification platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with key verticals such as financial services, healthcare, government contracting, or HR technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a high-growth or Series B/C/D+ stage company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling an outbound sales motion from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education and/or Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, Computer Science, or a related field; or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of progressive SaaS sales experience required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of sales leadership experience required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
