&lt;p&gt;ID.me is seeking a Senior Software Engineer, Front End to join the Applications team, building the &lt;strong&gt;SuperApp&lt;/strong&gt; — ID.me&#39;s web experience that helps members discover where their verified identity unlocks benefits, offers, and services across commerce, government, healthcare, and travel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role covers the SuperApp&#39;s customer-facing web surfaces, which include the Browser Extension along with other front-end experiences such as the Home Page, Life Events, and Government section. As team priorities evolve, this role may also extend into the broader &lt;strong&gt;ID.me Shop&lt;/strong&gt; web experience. &lt;strong&gt;This position will work from our Mountain View, CA office five days per week.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Maintain SuperApp Web Experiences:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and maintain the SuperApp&#39;s customer-facing web surfaces — including the Browser Extension&#39;s web-facing UI (content scripts, popup, in-page injected components) as well as other experiences like the Home Page and Life Events — using React and TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement Discovery &amp;amp; Offer Detection:&lt;/strong&gt; Build contextual offer discovery, coupon/cashback detection, and in-page notification patterns that surface relevant offers as members browse and shop online.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate with Platform APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate with Shopping Graph and Developer Portal APIs for merchant, offer, and eligibility data rather than hardcoding business logic client-side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extend into Shop as Needed:&lt;/strong&gt; Contribute to the broader ID.me Shop web experience alongside SuperApp surfaces as roadmap priorities evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with Design and Product:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Design and Product to turn discovery and personalization concepts into working, member-centered web UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, Accessibility &amp;amp; Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure shipped SuperApp features meet ID.me&#39;s standards for performance, accessibility, and cross-browser reliability (Chrome, Edge, Firefox).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide production support and maintenance for shipped features, including triaging and resolving incidents and bugs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong frontend engineering experience (typically 4+ years, or equivalent: 2+ years with a Master&#39;s degree)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or maintaining browser extensions (Chrome/Edge/Firefox), including content scripts, background/service workers, and Manifest V3&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid production experience with React (and Next.js) — required for adoption, not only for wrappers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
