&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ID.me is the next-generation digital identity wallet that simplifies how individuals securely prove their identity online. Consumers can verify their identity with ID.me once and seamlessly login across websites without having to create a new login and verify their identity again. Over 175 million users experience streamlined login and identity verification with ID.me at 22 federal agencies, 50 state government agencies, and more than 100 healthcare organizations. Over 600 consumer brands use ID.me to verify communities and user segments to honor service and build more authentic relationships. ID.me’s technology meets the federal standards for consumer authentication set by the Commerce Department and is approved as a NIST 800-63-3 IAL2 / AAL2 credential service provider by the Kantara Initiative. ID.me is committed to “No Identity Left Behind” to enable all people to have a secure digital identity. To learn more, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://network.id.me/&quot;&gt;https://network.id.me/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;ID.me is a full-time, in-office culture. Unless a specific job description explicitly states otherwise, all roles are on-site five days per week at one of our offices in McLean, VA; Mountain View, CA; New York City, NY; or Tampa, FL. Certain roles — such as field-based sales or other remote-by-design positions — may have different work arrangements as noted in their individual postings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At ID.me, we embrace the thoughtful use of AI tools in our daily work and there are even occasions where we leverage AI in our hiring process. However, during the interview process, we want to understand your individual skills and experiences. Therefore, we have guidelines on how AI can be appropriately used during your application and interviews which can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://insider.id.me/candidate-ai-use-in-interviewing/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ID.me is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer III&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;Developer Portal&lt;/strong&gt; team, where we&#39;re building the self-service platform that enables organizations to rapidly integrate id.me&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identity proofing is fundamentally complex. Integrating an identity proofing flow requires many steps while meeting standards-body assurance requirements. The Developer Portal is the product that brings those pieces together for the external developer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, much of that onboarding is still performed manually by in-house Solutions Consultants who have many other responsibilities. Our mission is to enable customers and their developers to register their application, configure their identity needs, test in a production-like sandbox, and launch to production all through a modern self-service experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;backend-leaning full-stack role&lt;/strong&gt;. You will spend most of your time designing and building the services, APIs, and data models behind the portal — application registration, authorization, and the developer-facing APIs our customers integrate against. You&#39;ll also ship the user-facing surfaces of those services power, working in our Next.js and React frontend to take features all the way to the customer rather than handing them off at the API boundary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own features end-to-end: from API contract through database schema, deployment, and production operation. You&#39;ll take defined problems, coordinate across teams to land them safely, and grow into technical ownership of the systems you build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our backend services are primarily &lt;strong&gt;Java (Spring Boot)&lt;/strong&gt; alongside legacy &lt;strong&gt;Ruby&lt;/strong&gt; services powering identity, organizations, applications, and authorization. The frontend is a micro-frontend platform built with &lt;strong&gt;Next.js&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;React&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt;. Previous Ruby experience is welcome but not required — we value engineers who are comfortable learning whatever technology the problem requires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in our &lt;strong&gt;Mountain View, CA&lt;/strong&gt; office five days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Build &amp;amp; Ship Self-Service Developer Features&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and implement Developer Portal capabilities end-to-end — from API contract design through database schema, frontend integration, and deployment. Independently drive small-to-medium features, coordinating with adjacent teams where your work crosses service boundaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Own API Contracts &amp;amp; Data Models&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the data models and REST API contracts for the capabilities you build, making deliberate decisions about backwards compatibility and versioning. Our customers integrate directly against these contracts, so changes must be additive and safe by default.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Authentication, Authorization &amp;amp; Identity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build secure Developer Portal capabilities spanning OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, enterprise SSO, multi-tenant authorization, relationship-based access control, session management, credential management, and identity-aware application provisioning. Partner with our Identity, Organizations, Authorization, and Platform Engineering teams to evolve these capabilities without disrupting existing integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Architecture, and platform teams to clarify requirements, surface risks early, and keep the developer experience coherent as the platform grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional software development experience building and operating production backend services. [Less for PhD, Master&#39;s]&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building backend services and REST APIs using a modern web framework such as Java (Spring Boot), Ruby on Rails, Node.js, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with relational databases, including authoring complex SQL and performing safe schema migrations against production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing REST API contracts, including versioning and backwards compatibility, and documenting them with OpenAPI or a similar specification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency with TypeScript and React — comfortable shipping customer-facing features through a modern frontend without requiring a frontend specialist to finish the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working familiarity with authentication and authorization concepts such as OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, or related identity standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience independently driving small-to-medium technical initiatives from definition through production, including cross-team coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with AI-assisted development tooling (e.g., Claude Code, Cursor) and a commitment to an AI-first engineering culture that leverages these tools to improve software quality, testing, and engineering velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, with experience partnering across Product, Design, and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built &lt;strong&gt;developer experience &lt;/strong&gt;as an explicit goal for example SDKs, API reference docs, quickstarts, sandbox or test environments, error messages and debugging surfaces, or self-serve onboarding flows and can speak to how it changed time-to-first-successful-integration for real external developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer-facing platforms such as developer portals, API platforms, authentication platforms, cloud platforms, payments platforms, or other self-service developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern Java (21+) and Spring Boot in production codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Ruby on Rails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PostgreSQL specifically, including graph-like or highly relational data models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Next.js, or with micro-frontend architectures such as Webpack Module Federation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise identity standards including OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, SAML 2.0, or SCIM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relationship-based authorization systems such as SpiceDB, OpenFGA, or Zanzibar-inspired architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy engines such as OPA or Cedar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing feature-flag-driven migrations in customer-facing production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with OpenAPI tooling, docs-as-code, or SDK generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity verification, fraud prevention, KYC/AML, or regulated identity systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of NIST 800-63 IAL/AAL guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Google Cloud Platform and cloud-native application development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability platforms such as OpenTelemetry, Honeycomb, Prometheus, and Sentry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated testing frameworks such as Playwright, Jest, or Cypress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup or high-growth company background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The annual base salary listed does not include a company bonus, incentive for sales roles, equity and benefits which will be determined based on experience, skills, education, relevant training, geographic location and role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;ID.me offers comprehensive medical, dental, vision, health savings account, flexible spending accounts (medical, limited purpose, dependent care, commuter benefit accounts), basic and voluntary life and AD&amp;amp;D insurance, 401(k) with company match, parental leave, ability to participate in unlimited paid time off subject to the terms and conditions of the PTO policy, including 8 company wide holidays, short and long-term disability insurance, accident and critical illness insurance, referral bonus policy, employee assistance program, pet insurance, travel assistant program, wellbeing and childcare discounts, benefit advocates, and a learning and development benefit.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Final offers may vary from the amount listed based on qualifications, professional experiences, skills, education, relevant training, geographic location, and other job related factors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Mountain View, CA and New York, NY Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$142,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$184,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;ID.me maintains a work environment free from discrimination, where employees are treated with dignity and respect. All ID.me employees share in the responsibility for fulfilling our commitment to equal employment opportunity. ID.me does not discriminate against any employee or applicant on the basis of age, ancestry, color, family or medical care leave, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, medical condition, national origin, physical or mental disability, political affiliation, protected veteran status, race, religion, sex (including pregnancy), sexual orientation, or any other characteristic protected by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances. ID.me adheres to these principles in all aspects of employment, including recruitment, hiring, training, compensation, promotion, benefits, social and recreational programs, and discipline. In addition, ID.me&#39;s policy is to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified employees who have protected disabilities to the extent required by applicable laws, regulations and ordinances where a particular employee works. Upon request we will provide you with more information about such accommodations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
