&lt;p&gt;ID.me is seeking a Staff Software Engineer, Full Stack to join the Commerce &amp;amp; Loyalty team, which owns the &lt;strong&gt;ID.me Shop&lt;/strong&gt; experience — cashback, affiliate offers, merchant discounts, and loyalty programs — along with the marketing and campaign surfaces that drive member engagement and commerce revenue. This position will work from our Mountain View, CA office five days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is full stack: you will spend significant time on the React/Next.js web experience across Shop and SuperApp, while also building and extending the backend services and APIs that power these features. You will be the technical anchor for the team&#39;s frontend surfaces, driving architecture decisions, raising the engineering bar, and partnering closely with Design and Product to translate commerce, personalization, and loyalty concepts into working member experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a product-focused role: your primary charter is deepening and scaling the Shop product experience itself, rather than owning shared platform or design-system infrastructure. Where patterns built for Shop are broadly useful, you may contribute reusable components back to ID.me&#39;s shared UI Foundations on an as-needed basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Maintain Shop Web Experiences:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and evolve the Shop front-end surfaces using React, Next.js, and TypeScript, including personalized offer discovery, cashback/loyalty flows, and merchant/store pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and Extend Backend Services:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and extend backend REST endpoints and services to support new or modified frontend features, taking full ownership from UI through backend rather than handing work to another team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate with Platform APIs:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate with Shopping Graph and Developer Portal APIs for merchant data, offer eligibility, and personalization signals rather than hardcoding business logic client-side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Infrastructure Modernization:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in ongoing platform work such as the GKE migration for Shop and adoption of shared UI patterns across the Shop codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to UI Foundations as Needed:&lt;/strong&gt; When a component or pattern built for Shop has broader applicability, contribute it back to ID.me&#39;s shared design system so other product teams can adopt it — without this becoming a primary focus of the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner Closely with Design and Product:&lt;/strong&gt; Work hand-in-hand with Design and Product to turn discovery, personalization, loyalty, and campaign/marketing concepts into feasible, member-centered web UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set Engineering Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Define patterns for testing, code quality, and review processes for the team&#39;s codebase; mentor other engineers on the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, Accessibility &amp;amp; Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure shipped features meet ID.me&#39;s standards for performance, accessibility, and cross-browser reliability; provide production support, including triaging and resolving incidents and bugs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong frontend engineering experience (typically 5+ years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in vanilla JavaScript, HTML, and the DOM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience shipping native Web Components in production (Custom Elements, templates, Shadow DOM, slots, events)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid production experience with React (and Next.js) — required for adoption, not only for wrappers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UI component libraries or design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with design tokens, theming, and scalable CSS (custom properties, shared stylesheets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven collaboration with design on system-level UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of accessibility standards and browser behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in a backend language for building and maintaining REST services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full stack ownership experience, from frontend UI through backend services and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native engineering practices — comfortable using AI tooling (e.g., code generation, test coverage, documentation) to accelerate development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;d Love to See&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ID.me&#39;s commerce/marketplace stack and shared internal design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with micro-frontend architectures or contributing to a shared internal design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building personalization, recommendation, offer-ranking, or loyalty/cashback UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with affiliate network integrations or e-commerce/marketplace platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity, benefits, or credential-based access concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The annual base salary listed does not include a company bonus, incentive for sales roles, equity and benefits which will be determined based on experience, skills, education, relevant training, geographic location and role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
